    "created_at": "2016-10-24T14:01:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-24T14:01:23Z",
    "body": "I am not sure this is actually a problem, the environment concept you're introducing seems to be fairly specialized and narrowly scoped, while media queries uses the term in a much more casual sense, also defined in a fairly fuzzy way, as what media queries evaluate about the page's environment can go from UA capabilities, to device characteristics, to user preferences, or questions about the physical environment.\n\nI don't know if HTML makes a specialized used of that MQ term, but from the point of view of the MQ spec itself, I think it is mainly a convenient plain English word to use to talk about the subject matter, rather than a term of art that should get a &lt;dfn> and be linked to, so I don't think it is a problem if the same word gets used for a different purpose elsewhere.\n",
